PTX LB-self+alias+async-bulk
"One thread reads shared d through its alias e, then a bulk copy writes d. A generic read is ordered before a later async-proxy write of the same address (D40), but a different virtual address behaves like a different proxy (8.6): without fence.proxy.alias the read may see the value of the later copy: allowed."
{
d=0 @cta 0;
e @ generic aliases d;
b=mbarrier(1) @cta 0;
g=1;
P0:r0=0;
P0:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                                                  ;
 ld.weak.shared::cta r0, e                                                 ;
 mbarrier.arrive.expect_tx.release.cta b, 1                                ;
 cp.async.bulk.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes d, g, b ;
 mbarrier.try_wait.parity.acquire.cta r1, b, 0                             ;
exists
(P0:r0 == 1)
